      ro: "Dallas, o metropola vibranta situata ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½n nordul statului Texas, este inima unui vast conglomerat economic care combina tehnologia, telecomunica?iile ?i finan?ele. Ini?ial un centru important pentru industria bumbacului ?i a petrolului dupa expansiunea re?elei feroviare ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½n anii 1870, ora?ul a evoluat ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½ntr-un hub corporativ major, gazduind numeroase companii din topul Fortune 500. Dallas este, din pacate, cunoscut ?i ca locul asasinarii pre?edintelui John F. Kennedy ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½n noiembrie 1963, eveniment comemorat la muzeul The Sixth Floor. Orizontul sau arhitectural este punctat de cladiri moderne ?i de emblematicul Reunion Tower. Aeroportul Interna?ional Dallas/Fort Worth, unul dintre cele mai mari ?i mai aglomerate din lume, sus?ine rolul sau de nod logistic esen?ial. Istorie K8 ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½ Statele Unite ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½n secolul XX.",
      en: "Dallas, a major metropolis in North Texas, serves as the economic and cultural hub of the Dallas-Fort Worth metroplex. Historically, the city developed as a critical center for the cotton and oil industries, significantly aided by its strategic position along major railroad lines. Today, Dallas boasts a highly diversified economy with major sectors in telecommunications, computer technology, banking, and transportation. The city's skyline is defined by striking modernist architecture, including the Reunion Tower and the Bank of America Plaza. Dallas is also culturally significant as the site of the tragic 1963 assassination of President John F. Kennedy, an event commemorated at the Sixth Floor Museum at Dealey Plaza. The city is a major transportation nexus, anchored by the massive Dallas/Fort Worth International Airport. History K8 ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½ mid-20th-century events and economic diversification."
