      en: "Pittsburgh is the second-largest city in Pennsylvania, uniquely situated at the confluence of the Allegheny and Monongahela rivers, which form the Ohio River. This strategic location propelled Pittsburgh into an industrial titan during the 19th and 20th centuries, most notably as the undisputed capital of the American steel industry, heavily driven by industrialists like Andrew Carnegie. Following the collapse of the domestic steel industry in the 1980s, which caused severe economic depression, Pittsburgh executed one of the most successful urban reinventations in the US. Today, its robust economy is anchored by healthcare, education, and advanced technology, particularly robotics and artificial intelligence, driven by the presence of Carnegie Mellon University and the University of Pittsburgh. Geography K8 ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½ post-industrial reinvention and river confluences."
