      ro: "Laredo, un ora? pozi?ionat adÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½nc ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½n sudul statului Texas, de-a lungul malului nordic al fluviului Rio Grande, este singurul ora? din Statele Unite sub care au fluturat pe rÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½nd ?apte steaguri diferite. Fondat ini?ial ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½n anul 1755 sub regimul spaniol, a reprezentat chiar capitala Republicii Independente Rio Grande pentru un scurt ?i tensionat an (1840). Loca?ia sa inegalabila la poarta de frontiera dintre SUA ?i Mexic ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½l face astazi un motor indispensabil al economiei nord-americane. Mai presus de orice, el este considerat cel mai vast port interior american, prelucrÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½nd lunar sute de mii de camioane ?i garnituri feroviare (incluzÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½nd podul esen?ial World Trade Bridge, construit ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½n 2000). Cultura locala celebreaza permanent festivalul ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½Zilele lui George WashingtonÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½ (Washington's Birthday Celebration), cel mai mare eveniment patriotic american dintr-o regiune predominant hispanica, fondat ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½n 1898. Geografie K7 ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½ grani?e, tratate NAFTA/USMCA ?i porturile terestre.",
      en: "Laredo is a prominent city in southern Texas, located directly on the north bank of the Rio Grande, opposite Nuevo Laredo, Mexico. The city's entire economic and cultural identity is defined by its position on the international border; Laredo operates as the largest inland port of entry in the United States and a critical conduit for massive volumes of international trade under agreements like USMCA. The constant flow of commercial trucking and rail traffic makes logistics, warehousing, and transportation the overwhelming pillars of the local economy. Culturally, Laredo is deeply intertwined with its Mexican sister city, boasting a population that is nearly entirely Hispanic, and heavily influenced by its historical origins as a Spanish colonial settlement founded in 1755. Geography K7 ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½ border towns and international logistics."
