      en: "Buffalo is the second-largest city in New York state, located at the eastern end of Lake Erie, adjacent to the Canadian border and near Niagara Falls. Historically, Buffalo was an industrial titan; the opening of the Erie Canal in 1825 transformed it into the primary gateway for commerce between the East Coast and the expanding Midwest. The city capitalized on its position by developing massive grain elevators, steel mills, and automobile manufacturing plants. Like many Rust Belt cities, Buffalo faced severe economic decline in the late 20th century. However, recent revitalization efforts have focused on healthcare, education, and leveraging its architectural heritage, which includes significant works by Frank Lloyd Wright and Louis Sullivan, alongside a distinct local culture famous for the invention of Buffalo wings. Geography K7 ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½ Great Lakes ports and Erie Canal history."
