      ro: "Jefferson City este capitala statului Missouri, desemnata ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½n mod special ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½n 1821 pentru aceasta func?ie datorita pozi?iei sale centrale de-a lungul fluviului Missouri. Numit ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½n onoarea celui de-al treilea pre?edinte al SUA, Thomas Jefferson, ora?ul a crescut ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½n jurul func?iilor guvernamentale. Cladirea masiva a Capitoliului sau din piatra de calcar domina o stÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½nca cu vedere spre fluviu ?i a fost completata ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½n 1917, remarcÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½ndu-se prin muralele interioare realizate de Thomas Hart Benton. Spre deosebire de St. Louis sau Kansas City, Jefferson City a pastrat un caracter administrativ ?i comercial mai lini?tit. Industria principala ramÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½ne guvernarea statala, completata de educa?ie prin Universitatea Lincoln, una dintre institu?iile istorice de culoare. Geografie K7 ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½ a?ezari fluviale.",
      en: "Jefferson City, colloquially known as 'Jeff City', is the capital of Missouri, strategically located centrally within the state on the southern bank of the Missouri River. Specifically selected as the capital site in 1821 while still an undeveloped wilderness, the city was named in honor of Thomas Jefferson. Its economy is heavily dependent on state government operations, which are the overwhelming primary source of employment. The city's skyline is dominated by the Missouri State Capitol, an impressive domed structure perched high on a bluff overlooking the river. Historically, Jefferson City was also defined by the presence of the massive Missouri State Penitentiary, once the largest maximum-security prison in the US, which now serves as a historical tourist attraction. Geography K7 ÃƒÂ¯Ã‚Â¿Ã‚Â½ planned capitals and river topography."
